# Git sync + branches

- After every task commit: push **`develop`**, then fast-forward promote **`test`**, then **`main`** (`develop → test → main`). Never leave those three out of sync after a finished task.
- Never leave local commits unpushed unless push fails — then report the error.
- Branches:
  - `main` — stable / defence-ready
  - `develop` — integration (default work branch)
  - `test` — experiments / WIP checks
- Default feature work: on `develop`. Promote to `test` then `main` after each completed task.
- Do not force-push `main` or `develop` unless the user explicitly asks.
